               </text>
            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your patient, a 67-year-old male, admitted on 26/08/2001 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Physical examination confirmed reduced air entry with expiratory wheeze bilaterally. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed mild hypoxaemia with hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and close monitoring of vital signs. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He is discharged in stable condition with adjusted inhaler therapy and a short course of oral prednisolone. Please arrange follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. I remain available for any queries.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
